# 2. PROJECT OVERVIEW

**Project Name:** FoodBridge AI

**Problem ID:** HACK-P197

**Category:** Food & Restaurant

**Project Type:** Student Hackathon Prototype

**Project Title:** Intelligent Food Donation and Redistribution Platform.

### Problem

Restaurants, hotels, bakeries, supermarkets, caterers, and community kitchens often have surplus edible food that may go to waste.

At the same time, NGOs, orphanages, homeless shelters, and charitable organizations need access to food donations.

There is a need for a centralized platform that connects donors with eligible recipients and coordinates food listings, requests, reservations, pickup schedules, and donation tracking.

### Solution

FoodBridge AI is an intelligent food redistribution platform that connects food donors with verified recipient organizations.

It enables donors to publish surplus food listings, helps NGOs discover suitable nearby donations, manages reservations, coordinates pickups, and tracks completed donations.

The platform uses AI-assisted matching, location-based discovery, automated recommendations, and impact analytics to improve food redistribution.

### Primary Objectives

- Reduce avoidable food waste.
- Connect food donors with eligible charitable organizations.
- Make available food and pickup information discoverable.
- Prevent double booking and missed collections.
- Simplify donation requests and pickup coordination.
- Track donations from listing to completion.
- Provide transparent operational and impact analytics.

