# 28. FINAL INSTRUCTIONS TO THE AI BUILDER

Start building FoodBridge AI as a completely new project.

Do not merely generate a design, mockup, or static dashboard.

Do not create buttons that have no functionality.

Do not use fake success messages in place of actual database operations.

Do not use frontend-only state as a substitute for backend persistence.

Do not hardcode dashboard statistics when database calculations are available.

Do not leave critical APIs unimplemented.

Do not silently ignore errors.

Do not claim external integrations are working without verifying them.

Do not expose private credentials.

Do not sacrifice backend reliability for decorative UI.

Prioritize a complete and reliable donor-to-recipient donation workflow before optional advanced features.

If the entire application cannot be completed in one execution, work phase by phase, preserve all completed work, and clearly identify the remaining tasks.

At every stage:
1. Implement the feature.
2. Connect it to the backend.
3. Connect it to the database.
4. Test its actual functionality.
5. Fix errors.
6. Continue to the next phase.

